[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_page")
id = &"welcome"
title = "What this is"
order = 10
summary = "Squads, a map with no edges, and who decides what."
body = "You command an army of SQUADS. A squad is the thing you click, order and
fight with — never an individual soldier. Every man in a squad walks where
the squad walks and fights who the squad fights, and the survivors close up
as casualties fall.

Everything happens on one seamless map that WRAPS. Walk far enough east and
you arrive from the west; the same north and south. There is no edge to back
against and no corner to be cornered in, which means there is no safe flank
anywhere on the map — only ground nobody has come round yet.

## The server decides

A match runs on a server, and the server is the authority on all of it: what
your troops can see, whether an order is legal, who wins a fight. Your screen
draws what it is told.

That is why an order can be refused, and why a refusal explains itself in a
line along the top. It is not the game failing — it is the authority
answering, and the answer is usually worth reading.

## Where to start

\"Your first minutes\" is the opening in order. It is short, and the opening is
the part of a match that is easiest to lose without noticing."
sources = Array[String](["res://decisions/D-002.md", "res://decisions/D-005.md", "res://decisions/D-008.md"])
